# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=conquest spec=rogue:assassination
# style=wander view=844x390,touch save=fresh.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl and playtest/plans/*.play first. rogue:assassination
# has been played nine times this job's history and every single one was
# mode=raid, mode=walk or mode=clear -- never a battleground. Conquest has
# seen `wander` exactly once before (2026-09-29-8.play, priest:shadow,
# desktop 1280x800): that body never engaged, took 78 total damage the whole
# match, and the match still ended in defeat (direction.md [[#7]]). Conquest
# also has an independent thread on melee/closing-distance: two different
# good-style casters (druid:balance, druid:restoration) both died at
# fightTime~9s beelining into the opening scrum, read as "conquest's own
# opening geometry punishes closing distance in the first ~9 seconds"
# (direction.md [[#7]], 2026-09-28).
#
# This cell crosses those two threads for the first time: a melee spec
# (rogue, the roster's fastest class per the #271 melee-evening finding)
# under `wander`, on the one map already flagged for punishing anyone who
# closes distance early, on a phone touch viewport nobody has used for
# `wander`+conquest before (prior pull was desktop). `wander` doesn't aim at
# the enemy cluster on purpose, but being a melee spec means any auto-attack
# it lands has to happen inside the same danger radius that killed the two
# casters -- this pull asks whether a melee body that "doesn't try" fails
# the same way the passive ranged pull did (#7's core shape) or the same way
# the closing-distance casters did (a third, distinct shape).

open
targets
shot front

tap battleground
targets
shot bg-menu

tap map:conquest
targets
shot conquest-picked

tap class:rogue:assassination
shot class-picked

tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot pulled
state
targets

play wander 90
shot mid1
state
bill
says

wait 5
play wander 90
shot mid2
state
bill

wait 5
play wander 90
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
